\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2  C.Bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2 , sells dollars   \b0\par\par\uc2 327 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Dezember 2007\par 17:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds reserves figure, other details)   \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Dec 27 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the interbank market, selling dollars at 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the Ukrainian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was pushed down to the lower depth of its permitted range, traders said on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 "There was continued high demand for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the interbank market and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in to sell dollars," said one dealer, saying trades had been conducted at 5.06/5.064.   \par \par \uc2 A top \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said, meanwhile, that foreign reserves had dipped slightly to $32.2 billion from a record high of $32.768 billion at the end of last month.   \par \par \uc2 First Deputy chairman Anatoly Shapovalov gave no reason for the slight decline.   \par \par \uc2 "We allowed no sharp fluctuations in the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he told reporters. "These were generally no more than one percent. The rate was generally favourable for exporters and the current figure of $32.2 billion is optimal."   \par \par \uc2 Dealers linked the dip to recent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The bank, which has maintained a narrow band for the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  of 5.00 to 5.06 since August 2005, has sold dollars on about 10 occasions in December.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers say increased demand for dollars has been prompted by the need to conclude import contracts, particularly purchases of energy, and an end-of-year outflow of portfolio investment.   \par \par \uc2 Reserves have risen by nearly $10 billion since the beginning of the year thanks to excess supply of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Over the first 11 months of the year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $7.774 billion in excess \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Shapovalov said he expected excess supply to remain on the market next year and would continue to consider chairman Volodymyr Stelmakh's proposal in October of expanding the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's narrow corridor. (Reporting by Natalya Zinets; Writing by Ron Popeski; Editing by Ruth Pitchford)   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 /\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071227e3cr000zv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
