\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2  cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2 , sells dollars at 5.06   \b0\par\par\uc2 281 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Dezember 2007\par 15:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (adds quote, background)   \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Dec 7 (Reuters) - The Ukrainian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars on Friday for the second time this week at 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within a narrow corridor of 5.00-5.06, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  again came into the market, selling the dollar at 5.06 ... Some banks with large demands refused to buy dollars that were more expensive and waited for the bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," one dealer said.   \par \par \uc2 This week's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are the first time the bank has sold dollars since April. Through much of May-September, the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  <UAH=> had been straining at its ceiling and the bank regularly bought dollars at 5.00 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Dealers have said demand for the dollar, already made scarcer after the global credit crunch, increased as businesses, especially energy firms, pay off their year-end bills.   \par \par \uc2 Last week, the bank had let the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  slip through the 5.06 floor but said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would correct itself because the movement was due to a single larger buyer of dollars.   \par \par \uc2 The bank has kept the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the 5.00-5.06 band since August 2005, within a longer-term range of 4.95-5.25, but has a stated aim of eventual greater flexibility.   \par \par \uc2 Dismissing speculation that the bank may make good on its promise soon, a senior official said no changes to the policy would be made before there is political stability. Politicians are yet to form a government two months after an election. (Reporting by Natalya Zinets; Editing by Mike Peacock)   \par \par \uc2 UKRAINE-\b \highlight22\uc2 HRYVNIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071207e3c70015u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
