\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine cbank to look at gas in '08  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  policy   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Sabina Zawadzki   \par \uc2 455 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Dezember 2007\par 17:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (adds quotes, analyst, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )   \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Dec 5 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday it would look into the impact of a higher 2008 gas import when considering alterations to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, a senior bank official said on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 First Deputy Chairman Anatoly Shapovalov also told Reuters the bank would make no moves until the end of the year to its policy of defending a narrow corridor of 5.00-5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the dollar, within a wider range of 4.95-5.25.   \par \par \uc2 "There will be no change to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy until the end of the year," Shapovalov said.   \par \par \uc2 "(Afterwards) we need to calculate how this new price will impact the demand for the dollar. By our calculations, demand for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will increase by about $2.7 billion."   \par \par \uc2 Ukraine signed an agreement with Russia's gas export monopoly  \uc2 Gazprom\uc2  on Wednesday to pay $179.50 per 1,000 cubic metres next year against $130 now.   \par \par \uc2 "It looks as though the (bank's) figure is simply based on the amount of gas imported this year and multiplied by the change in the average price between 2007-2008, without taking into account any possible effects from increased energy-use efficiency,"  \uc2 UniCredit\uc2  economist Simon Quijano-Evans said.   \par \par \uc2 Speculation had been mounting in recent months that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would make good on its long-stated objective of moving towards greater \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flexibility.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been straining at the 5.00 ceiling for much of the year, contained only by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  throughout May to September.   \par \par \uc2 But demand for the dollar has since increased as business, especially energy firms, paid year-end bills. The bank let the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  slip through the 5.06 floor late on Friday.   \par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, it sold dollars for the first time since April to bring it back into the band.   \par \par \uc2 Deputy Chairman Olexander Savchenko told a daily newspaper on Wednesday that the bank was getting ready to increase \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flexibility the moment there was some political stability in the country.   \par \par \uc2 Politicians have yet to form a government two months after a parliamentary election, the third vote in as many years, produced a shaky coalition of two parties linked to the 2004 pro-Western "Orange Revolution".   \par \par \uc2 Savchenko also dismissed the notion of moving away from a dollar corridor into other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  or a basket.   \par \par \uc2 "The first thing that discourages us from moving to a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket is that 80 percent of our external trade is tied to the dollar, including turnover from both the European Union and Russia," he said.   \par \par \uc2 UKRAINE-GAS/CBANK (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071205e3c5001as\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
