\par\par \b \uc2 UDPATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2  cbank fails to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  after  \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia \highlight\uc2  fall   \b0\par\par\uc2 292 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 2007\par 16:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds background)   \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Nov 30 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved outside the 5.00-5.06 band to the dollar, slipping to 5.067, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2 Since August 2005 the bank has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  within this narrow corridor, though it has a wider long-term band of 4.95-5.25 to the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 "Today was the first day when, thanks to rising demand (for the dollar), the 5.06 level was crossed but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," one dealer said.   \par \par \uc2 The bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy has prompted suggestions in recent weeks over whether it should stick to the corridor, modify or abandon it or create a reference basket of currncies.   \par \par \uc2 The head of the bank's council, Petro Poroshenko, said this month that the bank would stick to its wider band -- comments some analysts interpreted as signalling an easing of the tighter 5.00-5.06 band.   \par \par \uc2 Several analysts called for a revaluation several months ago, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly, buying up dollars at 5.00 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and as inflation soared beyond expectations.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chairman Volodymyr Stelmakh conceded in late October that revaluation would help the fight against inflation, which rose to 11.7 percent in the first 10 months of the year.   \par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has since weakened. Demand for the dollar is partly due to tighter liquidity stemming from the global credit crunch of the summer months and because importers are paying their year-end bills. (Reporting by Natalya Zinets; writing by Sabina Zawadzki; editing by David Stamp)   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 HRYVNIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071130e3bu00264\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
