\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine cbank to mull rate change after GDP data   \b0\par\par\uc2 352 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Oktober 2007\par 17:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates with details)   \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Oct 10 (Reuters) - Ukraine's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will wait until it has figures for economic growth for the first nine months of this year before deciding whether to raise interest rates to fight inflation, a top bank official said on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 Inflation rose 2.2 percent month-on-month in September fuelled by high food prices and rising wages and analysts expect it to top 10 percent by year-end. But the bank's monetary focus is on keeping the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stable, not on inflation.   \par \par \uc2 "We have a dilemma. If we raise the discount rate it will have an impact on production and economic growth. That is why we will see how GDP develops and after that we'll decide," the bank's First Deputy Chairman Anatoly Shapovalov told reporters.   \par \par \uc2 "If GDP slows down then we will not (raise rates)."   \par \par \uc2 The bank lowered the discount rate to 8.0 percent in July from 8.5 percent.   \par \par \uc2 The State Statistics Committee will release the nine-month gross domestic product data between Oct. 12 and Oct. 16.   \par \par \uc2 The economy has grown better than expected, accelerating to 7.5 percent in the first eight months of 2007, against 5.7 percent in the same period last year. Last year, inflation grew 11.6 percent.   \par \par \uc2 The government expects the economy to grow 6.5 percent in 2007, against growth of 7.1 percent last year, but Economy Minister Anatoly Kinakh said last month he saw growth matching last year's figure, or at about 7.0-7.2 percent.   \par \par \uc2 The government's forecast for inflation by the end of the year is 7.5 percent, but cumulative price rises for the first nine months of the year have overtaken that target, reaching 8.6 percent according to data released last Saturday.   \par \par \uc2 The bank keeps the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  within a narrow corridor of 5.0 to 5.06 to the dollar and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as required.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -RATES/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071013e3aa000ca\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
