\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine c.bank buys dollars 6th straight day   \b0\par\par\uc2 296 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juli 2007\par 13:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (adds quotes, background)   \par \par \uc2 KIEV, July 13 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday, buying excess dollars at 5.0 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the sixth consecutive trading day to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within a long-established corridor, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been buying dollars every day since last Friday and today was no exception," said one dealer.   \par \par \uc2 "Despite excess dollar supply, there is no obvious imbalance as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meets the demand of all sellers. There were no transactions lower than 5.0."   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has maintained the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a corridor of 5.0 to 5.06 to the dollar since August 2005, buying or selling dollars to keep the market steady.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said they held back from selling dollars below 5.0 in anticipation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's entry into the market.   \par \par \uc2 "We were buying in the morning at 5.001 and then selling at 5.0. I then tried to buy at 4.999, but there were no takers," said one dealer.   \par \par \uc2 Market participants predicted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would scale down \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  next week.   \par \par \uc2 "There were three big buyers this week, but I think the market will even out," said one dealer. "Demand has started to appear and sales have slowed."   \par \par \uc2 Dealers have linked increased dollar supply to an influx of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Ukrainian businesses intending to support political parties taking part in the September parliamentary election, aimed at ending months of political crisis in Ukraine.   \par \par \uc2 Top \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials last week ruled out any change in exchange rate policy, saying that would be particularly unwise given uncertainties surrounding the election.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 /\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070713e37d000zp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
