\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine c.bank buys dollars, 3rd straight day   \b0\par\par\uc2 317 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juli 2007\par 15:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (adds quotes, background)   \par \par \uc2 KIEV, July 10 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday, buying surplus dollars for the third straight trading day at 5.0 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within a long-established corridor, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2 "Most transactions occurred at 5.01/5.015 and it was initially hoped that the dollar would find support by the end of trading," said a dealer. "But many banks were selling, the dollar slipped and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was forced to buy."   \par \par \uc2 Ukraine's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been maintaining the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  within a corridor of 5.0-5.06 since August 2005 and periodically buys or sells dollars to maintain a balance.   \par \par \uc2 The bank last week said it had purchased a total of $658.4 million in June against $1.415 billion the previous month to steady the market.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the supply of excess dollars could be linked to borrowing by Ukrainian companies on international markets, purchases of Ukrainian treasury notes or to money flowing in ahead of a September parliamentary election.   \par \par \uc2 Dollar purchases in Ukraine are traditionally associated with large importers, particularly for energy purchases.   \par \par \uc2 One dealer suggested the market could find a new balance in the coming days at 5.02-5.03.   \par \par \uc2 "I think that with a cheaper dollar, buyers will start to appear and the market will even out, perhaps by the end of the week," the dealer said.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials said last week there were no grounds for any change in exchange rate policy in the immediate future.   \par \par \uc2 The head of the bank's council said any such change would be unwise given the uncertainty surrounding the election, intended to end months of turmoil pitting President Viktor Yushchenko against Prime Minister Viktor Yanukovich.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 /\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070710e37a001bg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
