\par\par \b \uc2 Ukraine C.Bank buys dollars at 5.0  \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 283 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juli 2007\par 18:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 KIEV, July 9 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the country's interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday for the second consecutive trading day, buying dollars at 5.0 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.   \par \par \uc2 "It was clear today from the start that there was a high supply of dollars, that importers were less active and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars," said one dealer.   \par \par \uc2 "There was very little movement, with transactions being struck close to 5.0."   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has since August 2005 maintained a corridor of 5.0 to 5.06 for the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , buying and selling dollars intermittently to keep the market balanced.   \par \par \uc2 Senior \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials, including chairman Volodymyr Stelmakh and council head Petro Poroshenko, last week dismissed as ungrounded speculation that the bank was considering a change in policy and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be revalued.   \par \par \uc2 Poroshenko said any change was unthinkable in conditions of uncertainty as Ukraine gears up for a September parliamentary election aimed at ending months of turmoil between President Viktor Yushchenko and Prime Minister Viktor Yanukovich.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week said it had purchased a total of $658.4 million in June against $1.415 billion the previous month to keep the market steady.   \par \par \uc2 "The situation on the market is stable," said another dealer. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  promised that the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  would stay within the corridor so it will stay there, perhaps until the New Year."   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said they expected high dollar supply to be maintained to reflect the interest of non-residents in a sale of treasury notes scheduled for Monday.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 /\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|M|D   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070709e379001kq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
