\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  to maintain  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  corridor   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Natalia Zinets   \par \uc2 336 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 2007\par 14:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, background)   \par \par \uc2 KIEV, June 22 (Reuters) - Ukraine's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday it intended to maintain a long-established corridor of 5.00-5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the dollar at least until the end of the year and expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to remain stable.   \par \par \uc2 "We forecast stability and know that there will be no sharp fluctuations and have no plans to change our current policy (until the end of the year)," the bank's First Deputy Chairman Anatoly Shapovalov told Reuters.   \par \par \uc2 Shapovalov added the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to buy a surplus of euros and other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  while demand and supply of dollars were currently balanced, enabling the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to maintain the 2-year-old dollar-\b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  corridor.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows from abroad have increased, Shapovalov said, notwithstanding political tensions in April and May over a decree by the president ordering a snap parliamentary election despite resistance from his arch rival, the prime minister.   \par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows have grown, 54 percent of all inflows come from export income, 21 percent -- from borrowing," he said.   \par \par \uc2 He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might decrease its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market only when \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2  started paying world prices for gas, a key demand of neighbour Russia.   \par \par \uc2 "We understand we should cut down on our \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  although they have not been that significant," he said.   \par \par \uc2 "But we can only do this when we move to world prices for gas, when there will be market feedback mechanisms, only then can we talk about a change in our exchange rate policy."   \par \par \uc2 A new round of negotiations on the price Ukraine pays Russia for gas is due soon. Ukraine pays $130 per 1,000 cubic metres of natural gas compared to an average price of $250 in western Europe.   \par \par \uc2 The price of imported gas is a major factor for Ukraine's economy, which is dominated by energy-intensive heavy industry.   \par \par \uc2 UKRAINE-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070622e36m000ye\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
