\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2 's c. bank prepared to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2 -dealers   \b0\par\par\uc2 430 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 April 2007\par 13:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (adds quote, details)   \par \par \uc2 KIEV, April 4 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is prepared to sell dollars at 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  if necessary, dealers said on Wednesday as political uncertainty intensified.   \par \par \uc2 President Viktor Yushchenko issued a decree this week to dissolve parliament and set a new election to stop a growing challenge to his authority from his rival, Prime Minister Viktor Yanukovich, who vowed to boycott the polls.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  <UAH=> slipped to 5.058-5.063 at 1022 GMT, closer to the weaker end of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trading band for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of 5.00-5.06 to the dollar. It was traded at around 5.03 to the dollar on Monday before the decree was issued.   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced its bid, making clear to us that it was ready to sell dollars if it was necessary," a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer in Kiev said.   \par \par \uc2 Another dealer said the market was calm.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps tight controls over the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently, both buying and selling foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  stable.   \par \par \uc2 Barring a major escalation of the conflict between Yushchenko and his rivals, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was set to remain stable as economic fundamentals are sound, dealers and economists said.   \par \par \uc2 "Some minimal fluctuations are possible on the market but they will be covered by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves which are over $23 billion", said Oleksander Suhonyako, head of Ukraine's banking association.   \par \par \uc2 Even if concerns grow over political instability, "the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will maintain \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability," he said.   \par \par \uc2 Yanukovich has refused to abide by the presidential decree and vowed to boycott the early parliamentary election set for May 27. Analysts expect the standoff to be resolved by talks and all sides to agree eventually to participate in the election.   \par \par \uc2 The conflict triggered a selloff in Ukrainian bonds and stocks this week, with the main PFTS index losing around 8 percent since the start of the week.   \par \par \uc2 "Amid all the negative political headlines, the Ukrainian economy continues to perform well," Tim Ash, an economist from Bear Stearns in London said in a research note after a trip to Ukraine this week.   \par \par \uc2 "Real GDP growth continues on a 6-7 percent trend rate, inflows of foreign direct investment continue to underpin the balance of payments ... As long as the linchpin of the Ukrainian economy, metals exports, remain strong, the economy should continue to perform well, providing reassurance for bond holders."   \par \par \uc2 UKRAINE-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070404e344000vy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
