\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Ukraine's c. bank buys dollars for 1st time in 2007  \b0\par\par\uc2 361 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2007\par 15:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds more comment)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, March 12 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday, buying dollars for the first time this year at a rate of 5.00 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the dollar, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The bank has sold dollars several times this year. It has also bought pounds and euros to replenish reserves.  \par \par \uc2 "Loads of dollars were on the market today due to the holiday weekend. Exporters' revenues had accumulated," a dealer in Kiev said. "The market could not absorb everything and some were forced to sell to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."  \par \par \uc2 Ukrainian markets had been closed since last Thursday to celebrate International Women's Day.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps tight control over the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly, buying and selling foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  within 5.00-5.06. It has been defending these levels for about two years.  \par \par \uc2 Oleksander Savchenko, deputy head to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor, said the bank would wait for more political stability before implementing a long-delayed plan to allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  greater flexibility.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials have previously said the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's band could be expanded to 4.95-5.25 to the dollar this year, but gave no exact timeframe for the decision.  \par \par \uc2 Political activity is plagued by a battle for powers between President Viktor Yushchenko and Prime Minister Viktor Yanukovich, rivals from the 2004 Orange Revolution. But the economy is robust and has so far shrugged off the uncertainty.  \par \par \uc2 "We believe that eventually when the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is allowed to float, its trend bias would be for stronger levels," UBS investment bank said in a research note.  \par \par \uc2 "Strong exports of steel, chemicals, natural gas and soft commodities have provided a growth boost for Ukraine. A small current account deficit is covered by strong foreign direct investment."  \par \par \uc2 Dealers expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to open at about 5.01-5.02 to the dollar on Tuesday compared with 5.045-5.05 per dollar at Monday's opening.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 /\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070312e33c001he\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
