\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine's c.bank sells dollars for 3rd time in week  \b0\par\par\uc2 280 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Januar 2007\par 13:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, more comment)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Jan 19 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday, selling dollars at 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the third time this week, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was selling yesterday and it is again selling today at 5.06 (\b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the dollar)," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 "We have bought some from the market and some from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."  \par \par \uc2 Anatoly Shapovalov, first deputy chairman of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , told Reuters in an interview on Thursday the bank was ready to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  if there was a distortion between supply and demand.  \par \par \uc2 He said the bank had no immediate plans to change its \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  corridor of 5.00-5.06 to the dollar which it has defended for about two years.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  started sliding late last week, breaking through the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's support level due to growing dollar demand from oil products importers and borrowers needing to service loans. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said the slide was short-term.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said Shapovalov's comments have calmed the market. The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  <UAH=> was traded at about 5.06 per dollar on Friday compared with about 5.07 per dollar earlier this week.  \par \par \uc2 "Some people tried to push quotes to 5.07 (\b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the dollar). But I do not think they succeeded. The main thing was to wait for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," one \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader in Kiev said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to open at 5.06-5.065 to the dollar next week.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 /\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070119e31j0014c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
