\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Ukraine c. bank sells dollars, 1st time since Dec 1  \b0\par\par\uc2 309 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Januar 2007\par 15:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds c. bank comment)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Jan 16 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, selling dollars at 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time since Dec. 1.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's statements that it will not allow sharp fluctuations have hereby been confirmed," Valery Lytvytsky, a senior adviser to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chairman, told Reuters.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  saw that the hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  demand was outpacing (supply) and came into the market."  \par \par \uc2 He gave no details on the amount sold on Tuesday. Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not covered demand entirely.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  <UAH=> started sliding last week on tight dollar supply at the start of the year, breaking through the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's support level of 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  today but the demand accumulated in previous days was not fully met because the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has certain limits on each bank," one dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded at around 5.065-5.070 on Tuesday compared with about 5.04 per dollar last week. Dealers expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to regain some ground thanks to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  support and to trade up at about 5.062-5.065 to the dollar on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has helped today. But still it did not cover all demand. This means that tomorrow the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be quoted up, but still lower than the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's level," another dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has defended the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  corridor of between 5.00-5.06 to the dollar for about two years.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last sold dollars on December 1. It also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  several times since then to buy dollars.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 /\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070116e31g002lc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
