\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine's c. bank buys dollars for 2nd day  \b0\par\par\uc2 287 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Dezember 2006\par 16:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds dealer comments)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Dec 20 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Wednesday, buying dollars at 5.00 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the second trading day in a row, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps a close watch over the market and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly, both buying and selling dollars, to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  within 5.00-5.06 to the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in again today. But it seems a short-term trend related to the end of the year payments," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 "There are no drastic changes in the economy so in January we may see another picture."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has started strengthening since the start of the week, helped by higher exporters' sales at the end of the year as well as hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flowing in as a result of active corporate and sovereign borrowing.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  <UAH=> was traded at 5.0050/5.0135 to the dollar in the afternoon trade compared with 5.02/5/025 at the opening.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has defended the 5.00-5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the dollar corridor for over a year already.  \par \par \uc2 It was selling dollars in the first four months of the year to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  from political instability linked to a parliamentary poll but then it switched to purchases in May.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials have promised they would allow more flexibility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  from next year. They have announced plans to expand the corridor to 4.95-5.25 to the dollar in 2007 but exact timing is yet to be announced.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 /\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020061220e2ck0020o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
