\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine C.Bank sells dollars, 1st time since July  \b0\par\par\uc2 286 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Dezember 2006\par 16:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds quotes, background)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Dec 1 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prop the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday, selling dollars at 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 , its first such sales since July 28.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the bank stepped in to stem demand for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , particularly for contracts for energy purchases.  \par \par \uc2 They said parliament's dismissal of two ministers allied to pro-Western President Viktor Yushchenko had no effect on the market.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  had slipped in trading to 5.06/5.07 against 5.05 on Thursday before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in.  \par \par \uc2 "Even compared to Thursday, there was very little (dollar) supply. Demand was outstripping it considerably," said one dealer.  \par \par \uc2 Market participants said it was difficult to predict how long high dollar demand would last.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deputy head Oleksandr Savchenko told Reuters on Thursday that the market would remain balanced into the New Year despite certain rises in the price of imported gas.  \par \par \uc2 Ukraine in 2005 paid $95 per 1,000 cubic metres of gas against $50 previously, but the change had little effect on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. Prices are expected to climb to $130 in 2007.  \par \par \uc2 Savchenko said greater demand for dollars would be offset by an inflow of direct investment, credits and borrowings.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate has been fixed at 5.05 to the dollar for over a year as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  maintains a close watch on the market.  \par \par \uc2 The bank sold \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  early this year to offset instability linked to a March election, but has bought about $2.2 billion since May.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 / \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020061201e2c1001gz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
