\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine's c. bank reserves rise to year-high  \b0\par\par\uc2 371 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Oktober 2006\par 16:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds more details, comment, wraps \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Oct 30 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gross hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose to a 2006 high of $19.4 billion as of October 30 due to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases on the interbank market, bank officials said on Monday. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chairman Volodymyr Stelmakh said the bank had replenished the $2.1 billion sold from reserves in the first four months of the year to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  from political instability linked to a March parliamentary election.  \par \par \uc2 "We have completely replenished the amount of reserves," he told Reuters.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials said the level compared with $19.395 billion at the start of January. Reserves stood at $19.238 billion as of October 19.  \par \par \uc2 "This event deserves attention together with other events -- an improving balance of payments and fiscal balance," said Valery Lytvytsky, a senior adviser to Stelmakh.  \par \par \uc2 "...Despite a traditional seasonal volatility, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves will not slip this year, but will grow. These macroeconomic signals -- balance of payments, fiscal balance and hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves are a basis for stability."  \par \par \uc2 Ukraine imports up to 80 percent of its energy resources and in autumn demand for hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traditionally rises due to growing imports of gas and oil.  \par \par \uc2 But the situation this year has proved different due to a steady inflow of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from exporters and Ukrainian companies borrowing abroad.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought about $300 million so far this month compared with $552.5 million in September. It bought a total of $2.2 billion in May to October. In January to April, the bank sold $2.1 billion.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps close watch over the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently, buying and selling hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  within a target corridor of 5.00-5.06 to the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday for the first time this month to buy dollars, but the amount was a modest $17 million.  \par \par \uc2 It bought hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier this month, but most transactions were in euros and pounds and in small amounts, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials said.  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-UKRAINE-RESERVES (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020061102e2au00222\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
