\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Gas deal to keep Ukraine  \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia \highlight\uc2  stable -c.bank  \b0\par\par\uc2 311 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 2006\par 09:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds details, comment)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Sept 28 (Reuters) - A deal struck between Ukraine and Russia to hold gas import prices steady through to the end of this year should keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stable, a senior Ukrainian central banker said on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 "We forecast that the exchange rate will be stable and fluctuations will be no greater than one percent," said Anatoly Shapovalov, first deputy chairman of the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently, both buying and selling hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  within a range of 5.00-5.06 to the dollar. It has defended these levels for more than a year already.  \par \par \uc2 Russia's gas giant Gazprom said earlier this week that gas prices for Ukraine will not change until next year despite a sharp increase in prices Gazprom is paying for buying gas from Central Asia.  \par \par \uc2 Gazprom said Ukraine will continue to receive gas at a price of $95 per 1,000 cubic metres in the fourth quarter, while talks about prices in 2007-2009 will be completed by the year-end.  \par \par \uc2 Shapovalov added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had bought $438 million via \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the beginning of September, increasing its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to over $19 billion.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hopes to increase its reserves by a further $300-400 million this year compared with their levels at the start of the year, he said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gross hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves stood at their record high of $19.4 billion in January.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  then sold $2.1 billion between January to April to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  from political instability linked to parliamentary elections in March, but switched to purchases in May.  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-UKRAINE-CBANK (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060928e29s000yk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
