\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine's c.bank buys dollars for 2nd day running  \b0\par\par\uc2 262 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2006\par 13:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds details, background)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Sept 21 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday, buying dollars at 5.0 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the second consecutive trading day, dealers said, as dollar supply far outweighed demand.  \par \par \uc2 "Supply was far ahead of demand. There were plenty of sellers and dollar rates were beginning to fall quickly," said one dealer.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently, both buying and selling hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , keeping the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  for more than a year now within a band of 5.00-5.06 to the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the dollar had fallen by midday to 5.002 from early morning levels of 5.016/5.024.  \par \par \uc2 "Why was there mass selling? It could simply have been a set of circumstances, like contracts being closed," said the dealer.  \par \par \uc2 "There could also be an external factor. The U.S. Federal Reserve left key rates untouched, but said they could subsequently be lowered. After that, the euro began rising and the dollar weakened."  \par \par \uc2 Officials have previously said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may buy about $1 billion on the interbank market to replenish its reserves.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $2.1 billion in January to April -- initially to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  from political instability linked to a March election which spawned four months of instability over the formation of a coalition government.  \par \par \uc2 But it switched to purchases in May, buying around $1.8 billion since then.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060922e29m000wf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
