\par\par \b \uc2 Ukraine's reserves up to $19.01 bln on bond issue  \b0\par\par\uc2 264 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 2006\par 17:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Sept 21 (Reuters) - Ukraine's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  gross hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves grew to $19.010 billion as of September 21 compared with $18.697 billion at the end of August following a successful bond placement and continued dollar purchases.  \par \par \uc2 "As of September 21 the reserves are over $19 billion... We have practically recovered the $2.1 billion we lost in the first and second quarters," Valery Lytvytsky, chief adviser to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chairman, told Reuters.  \par \par \uc2 "I think that in October-November we will again see the record high of $19.390 billion which we had on January 1."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $2.1 billion from its reserves in January to April to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  against instability linked to a March parliamentary election that produced four months of political deadlock.  \par \par \uc2 But it switched to purchases in May, buying about $1.8 billion on the interbank market in nearly daily \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday, buying dollars at 5.0 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government also placed 12-year bonds worth 384 million Swiss francs ($307 million) earlier this month.  \par \par \uc2 Lytvytsky urged the government to borrow more, saying conditions were favourable.  \par \par \uc2 "We received this $300 million in the reserves. It improves prospects for achieving a record high," he said.  \par \par \uc2 "The government will be doing the right thing if it borrows again while the Federal Reserve and central banks have not started raising rates. This pause plays in our favour."  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-UKRAINE-RESERVES|LANGEN|ABN|M|D  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060921e29l001x6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
