\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine c. bank buys dlrs for third time in week  \b0\par\par\uc2 290 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 2006\par 14:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds details, more comments)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Aug 18 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday, buying dollars at 5.00 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the third time this week, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 "The dollar is abundant on the market," a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer in Kiev said. "August is a traditionally slower month for business when many are on holidays. But exporters sell their hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  earning actively and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buys it all out."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday and Thursday this week.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  <UAH=> has started to strengthen at the start of the month after the parliament approved a new government under Prime Minister Viktor Yanukovich on Aug. 4, ending a four-month political crisis.  \par \par \uc2 Lower business activities amid summer holidays have also cut demand for dollars and pushed the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  up, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said they expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to continue dollar purchases next week.  \par \par \uc2 "I do not see any reasons for the current situation to change. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue dollar purchases," one dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought over $1 billion since May and plans to buy another $1 billion in August and September, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials have said.  \par \par \uc2 The bank tracks fluctuations on global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently, both buying and selling dollars, to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  at between 5.00-5.06 to the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The bank sold around $2.1 billion in January to April to defend the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from political instability amid prolonged talks over a new coalition government. It then switched to dollar purchases in May.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060818e28i0010h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
