\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine's c.bank buys dollars for 2nd time in week  \b0\par\par\uc2 318 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 August 2006\par 14:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds government comment)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Aug 17 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Thursday, buying dollars at 5.00 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the second time this week, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  <UAH=> strengthened to 5.0000/5.0030 to the dollar in afternoon trade. Demand for dollars is traditionally lower in August as business activity slows when many in \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2  are on holiday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps a close watch over the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently, both buying and selling hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a range between 5.00-5.06 to the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 It has been defending these levels for about a year.  \par \par \uc2 President Viktor Yushchenko met \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chairman Volodymyr Stelmakh on Thursday and praised the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stability which had helped attract foreign investment and issue more long-term bank loans to producers.  \par \par \uc2 "They noted positive trends in the economy laid out by the previous government and the need for the current cabinet to ensure continuity," Yushchenko's press service said.  \par \par \uc2 "The president and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chairman noted a balance in foreign investment, stressing that a stable national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a key factor for its influx."  \par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, parliament appointed a new government led by Prime Minister Viktor Yanukovich, ending a four-month political crisis.  \par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Mykola Azarov, has pledged to cooperate with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to secure a stable and predictable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  plans to expand the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's corridor to 4.95-5.25 to the dollar in 2007 from 5.00-5.06 per dollar this year.  \par \par \uc2 Yushchenko held the post of central banker in 1993-99 and oversaw the introduction the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060817e28h0012q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
