\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Ukraine c. bank sees no reasons for weaker  \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Olena Horodetska  \par \uc2 467 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 2006\par 12:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds c. bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Aug 14 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange rate is balanced and there are no reasons for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken as the government forecast a foreign trade surplus for 2007, a top \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 "There are no reasons for a \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluation under a forecast surplus on foreign trade. We think the rate is balanced as of today," First Deputy Chairman Anatoly Shapovalov told reporters after a government meeting which discussed macroeconomic forecasts for 2007.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  <UAH=> has been fixed at 5.05 to the dollar for about a year.  \par \par \uc2 Ukraine's economy is export-driven and global markets for steel and chemicals -- the country's key export products -- have started to improve in recent months. Outlook for next year is also favourable.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has strengthened this month as parliament approved Prime Minister Viktor Yanukovich ending a four-month political crisis. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has increased the frequency of its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  this month to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's appreciation.  \par \par \uc2 On Monday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars at 5.00 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a second trading day in a row. Last week the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stayed away from the market only on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to remain stable in the near term at least until the current \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  management is in place," a dealer said. "President (Viktor Yushchenko) as a former central banker will not allow anything."  \par \par \uc2 Shapovalov said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had bought over $1 billion to its reserves in the last three and a half months. It sold $2.1 billion in January to April to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  from political instability linked to a parliamentary election in March.  \par \par \uc2 Some economists have feared the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  would start to weaken later in the year due to a growing demand for dollars from importers of fuel and gas during autumn and winter months. Yanukovich has also promised to defend exporters, a policy which may include a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Shapovalov said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the government agreed "to cooperate to ensure low inflation, stable exchange rate and a modest budget deficit to create a more favourable investment climate" next year.  \par \par \uc2 The government used the rate of 5.1 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the dollar to calculate the budget for next year, he said. He also confirmed \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's plans to expand the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's corridor to 4.95-5.25 to the dollar for 2005 compared with 5.00-5.06 to the dollar for this year and expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fluctuate at the interbank market.  \par \par \uc2 "Fluctuations within 1 percent is normal for the market," he said.  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-UKRAINE-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060814e28e000qz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
