\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-INTERVIEW-Ukraine's c.bank may buy $1 bln for reserves  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Natalya Zinets  \par \uc2 546 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 2006\par 11:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds c. bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Aug 11 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought $103 million in the interbank market so far in August and may buy another $1 billion in the next two months, Valery Lytvytsky, a senior adviser to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chairman, said on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The bank keeps a close watch over the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently, buying and selling dollars to defend a de facto dollar peg of 5.00-5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the dollar. The official rate is 5.05.  \par \par \uc2 "In the first quarter, we lost two billion (dollars) but by now we have returned a considerable part ... I think we can have $1 billion from the market in the next two months," he told Reuters in a telephone interview.  \par \par \uc2 "It is unlikely we will have an outflow of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in September because metal exports are forecast as relatively good. In October-November, certain volatility is possible but in any case reserves will not be lower than $18 billion."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $2.1 billion in the first four months of the year to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  from political uncertainty linked to a parliamentary election. It then switched to dollar purchases, buying about $807 million from May to July.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Lytvytsky said the bank had already bought $103 million in the interbank market so far in August. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  nearly daily this week as the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has started to strengthen after parliament approved Viktor Yanukovich as Ukraine's new prime minister, ending a four-month political crisis.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was again buying dollars at 5.00 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stayed away from the market only on Thursday this week.  \par \par \uc2 Some economists expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to come under downward pressure next month when dollar demand grows due to the need to import more fuel.  \par \par \uc2 Yanukovich's government, led by his pro-Russian Regions Party, has also promised to support exporters, a policy which may include a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Exporters account for about 60 percent of Ukraine's gross domestic product and are a major source of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  earnings.  \par \par \uc2 Lytvytsky said high \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and good outlook for Ukrainian exporters gave no grounds for discussion about the need to devalue the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has repeatedly said it was committed to keeping the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stable. Its reserves stood at $18.101 billion at the end of July. The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been fixed by the bank at 5.05 to the dollar for about a year already.  \par \par \uc2 Lytvytsky said he expected the new government to work to support economic growth.  \par \par \uc2 "We should support the government in its intentions to cut budget deficit, review tariffs policies and in their statements about staying away from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary and credit policy," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Yanukovich told his first news conference on Thursday that his government wanted to review the 2006 budget and cut the deficit. His finance minister, Mykola Azarov, promises to cut taxes and has said the exchange rate should be "stable, predictable and justified".  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-UKRAINE-RESERVES (UPDATE 2, INTERVIEW)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|NAT|BNX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060814e28b000ni\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
