\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine's c.bank buys dollars for 2nd day running  \b0\par\par\uc2 311 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 August 2006\par 15:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Aug 8 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday, buying dollars at 5.00 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the second trading day in a row, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought some dollars as the market was awash with dollars again today following the easing of the political situation. Political risks are over for now," said one dealer in Kiev.  \par \par \uc2 "Today I would say it's business as usual: the country is working, the economy is working, trading is active and market volumes are as normal."  \par \par \uc2 Most deals were done on Tuesday at about 5.002/5.010 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 , mostly unchanged from Monday's levels.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have to buy more dollars by the end of the week.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has started to strengthen against the dollar following the decision of Ukraine's parliament to approve Viktor Yanukovich as new prime minister, ending a four-month political crisis.  \par \par \uc2 However, economists said the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  would come under pressure next month when demand for dollars traditionally grows in Ukraine due to the need to import more fuel.  \par \par \uc2 Yanukovich's government, led by his pro-Russian Regions party, has also promised to support exporters, a policy which may include a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "We anticipate that the Regions of Ukraine will prove to be an effective pro-business government with policies particularly aimed at favouring Ukraine's major exporters," JP Morgan investment bank said in a note.  \par \par \uc2 "This bias may well mean a delay in WTO membership and some weakening of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  during this autumn when there is a high seasonal demand for hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ... JPMorgan expects the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to end this year at 5.20 (to the dollar)."  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060808e288001np\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
