\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine c.bank buys dollars as  \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia \highlight\uc2  rises  \b0\par\par\uc2 387 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 August 2006\par 15:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds dealers', Azarov quotes, details, background)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Aug 7 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the first time in two weeks on Monday, buying dollars at 5.00 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the new government's call for a stable exchange rate, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  <UAH=> strengthened against the dollar over the last two trading days following Ukraine's parliament decision to approve Viktor Yanukovich as new prime minister that ended a four-month crisis over the government.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded at about 5.00 to the dollar in afternoon trade compared with 5.024 at the opening. It traded at around 5.06 to the dollar last week.  \par \par \uc2 "Today the market was unable to cope on its own, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to buy dollars. The government appointment became a signal that the dollar will not rise in the near-term," one dealer in Kiev said.  \par \par \uc2 "People started to sell (dollars) late last week. Then the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened by about 2 kopecks. Everybody who had long positions got scared and rushed to sell today."  \par \par \uc2 Yanukovich, defeated by President Viktor Yushchenko after the Orange Revolution in 2004, returned to power as his pro-Russian Regions party won a parliamentary election in March. He was finally approved by parliament on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Mykola Azarov, Yanukovich ally and finance minister in the new government, called on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support economic growth by pursing a competitive exchange rate policy, saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate should be "stable, predictable and justified".  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps a close watch over the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently, both buying and selling hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  within a corridor of 5.00-5.06 to the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 It has been defending these levels for about a year.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $2.1 billion in the first four months of the year when the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  was hit by political uncertainty around the parliamentary election in March and subsequent talks on forming a new coalition government.  \par \par \uc2 In May, the bank switched to purchases, buying about $800 million in the last three months.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was last seen buying dollars on July 24.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060807e2870019b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
