\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine c. bank sells dollars, 1st time in 3 mths  \b0\par\par\uc2 396 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juli 2006\par 14:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds dealer comment, details)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, July 28 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday, selling dollars at 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time since April, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  <UAH=> has started sliding this week due to protracted uncertainty over Ukraine's new coalition government which is still incomplete after four-months of talks.  \par \par \uc2 "Dollar demand was strong and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to cover it," one dealer in Kiev said.  \par \par \uc2 "Uncertainty is high ... Many people lack patience. The future is unclear. Nobody knows who will head the government and what we should expect."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  slipped to 5.057/5.063 on Friday compared with 5.046/5.05 on Thursday. The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was traded at about 5.02 to the dollar at the start of the week.  \par \par \uc2 Downward pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has intensified this week after deputies failed to form a government within the 60 days set out in the constitution.  \par \par \uc2 President Viktor Yushchenko can now dissolve the parliament but so far he has proved reluctant to do it and called for more talks.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said continued support from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would help to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  stable in the near term but they hoped for a quick resolution of the parliamentary crisis.  \par \par \uc2 Yushchenko has until Aug. 3 to decide whether to bow to his opponents and appoint his old rival Viktor Yanukovich -- the man he defeated in the Orange Revolution -- or dissolve parliament.  \par \par \uc2 Valery Lytvytsky, a top adviser to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chairman, said this week he expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to remain stable at about 5.05 to the dollar by the end of the year due to quicker economic growth, low inflation and high \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserves.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has defended the 5.05 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate to the dollar since August 2005. It \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly, both buying and selling dollars, to support the stability.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was selling dollars in the first months of the year to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  from political uncertainty ahead of parliamentary elections in March.  \par \par \uc2 It then switched to dollar purchases. The bank bought about $808 million in May to July compared with sales of $2.1 billion in January to April.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060728e27s001e1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
