\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine's c.bank resumes dollar purchases  \b0\par\par\uc2 396 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juli 2006\par 16:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds quotes)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, July 24 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  resumed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday, buying dollars at 5.00 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has kept the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  between 5.00-5.06 per dollar since August 2005, intevening regularly by both buying and selling dollars.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is again buying dollars at 5.0. But on the market there are loads of people willing to buy at 5.02 or at 5.01. The volumes they are offer are good -- tens of millions. But somebody is still selling directly to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," one dealer in Kiev said.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said state companies which take on foreign loans were likely to work directly with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Ukraine's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market lacks transparency. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps a close watch on the market and is willing to buy dollars as much as possible to replenish reserves, hit by political uncertainty at the start of the year.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $2.1 billion from its reserves in January to April to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  both before and after a March parliamentary election which has plunged Ukraine into political turmoil.  \par \par \uc2 But from May, it switched to dollar purchases since May, buying $491.4 million in May and June.  \par \par \uc2 Four months after the election, Ukraine lacks a working government and parliament but the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains stable, largely because of lower business activity in the summer months.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also repeatedly expressed its commitment to a stable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Dealers expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slide in the autumn if Viktor Yanukovich, leader of the Regions Party, becomes prime minister. The Moscow-friendly party leads a prospective coalition cabinet with two leftist groups and proposed Yanukovich as premier last week.  \par \par \uc2 President Viktor Yushchenko, who defeated Yanukovich in the presidential election after the Orange Revolution in 2004, is considering whether to submit Yanukovich's nomination to parliament. The assembly must then approve it.  \par \par \uc2 The Regions party includes many businessmen and industrialists whose major assets are in Ukraine's exporting industries. They back a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is probably willing to show that everything is under control. But the political configuration is changing. It may bring depreciation," one dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060724e27o001aa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
