\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine's C.Bank buys dollars second straight day  \b0\par\par\uc2 326 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Juni 2006\par 13:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds more comment)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, June 30 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday, buying dollars at 5.0 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the second day in a row as dealers reported increased supply of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from exporters.  \par \par \uc2 "The dollar rose a bit in the morning to 5.01/5.02, but towards the end of trading, supply rose sharply and you could buy dollars practically without difficulty at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate of 5.0," said one dealer.  \par \par \uc2 "Without doubts these are exporters' earnings. The steel is traded very well at the moment. Exporters are concluding contracts at a new, higher price. It is caused by changes on the world markets," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers also said the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in demand at the end of the month due to tax payments and tighter liquidity.  \par \par \uc2 Rates on overnight credits jumped to between 11 and 14 percent on Friday from around 4-7 percent in the previous trading day.  \par \par \uc2 "Now, few people are selling funds. Many like us, for example, cannot afford to sell free \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It should remain on the corresponding accounts and it pushed the rates," another dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  usually checks how commercial banks meet their requirements on obligatory reserves at the end and at the start of each month. Many companies are also paying value-added tax to the state budget at the end of the month.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said banks' balances in their correspondent accounts, a liquidity indicator, fell to 9.776 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  as of June 30 compared with 10.628 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the start of the month.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to continue dollar purchases next month.  \par \par \uc2 "The situation on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is likely to remain the same unless something outrageous happens," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060630e26u000yt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
