\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine's c. bank resumes dollar purchases  \b0\par\par\uc2 240 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juni 2006\par 14:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds more comment)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, June 29 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Thursday, buying dollars at 5.0 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the second time this week as demand for \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained high due to tax payments, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 "From the 20th up until the end of the month, various tax payments are planned. All \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  are going to the state treasury," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps a close watch on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently, both buying and selling hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  within a corridor of 5.00-5.06 per dollar. It has defended these levels since August 2005.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the bulk of the deals were concluded between 5.0180-5.0220.  \par \par \uc2 "The market situation is interesting. The dollar was trading high but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was still buying out. Some large clients are probably selling most of their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," another dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to continue dollar purchases through the week.  \par \par \uc2 Companies pay value added tax at the end of each month. Banks' balances in their correspondent accounts at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , an indicator of liquidity, slipped to 9.448 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  ($1.87 billion) on Thursday from 10.084 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  the previous day.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060629e26t000yl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
