\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine's c.bank buys dollars for 3rd day  \b0\par\par\uc2 331 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 2006\par 14:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds comment, details)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, June 22 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Thursday, buying dollars at 5.0 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the third day in a row, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The market mostly ignored the conclusion of a coalition agreement -- after three months of divisive talks -- by parties backing Ukraine's 2004 "Orange Revolution".  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  between January and April, but switched to purchases in May and June. This month, the frequency of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been higher than in May.  \par \par \uc2 "The scenario is similar to yesterday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars at 5.0. Most deals were done within the range of 5.0015-5.0025," one dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 Most deals with the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  <UAH=> were concluded at about 5.003/5.0045 on Wednesday, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy out dollars.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the higher frequency of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars in June was caused by lower demand for hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from importers.  \par \par \uc2 Ukraine's major imports -- energy resources -- traditionally decline in the summer months.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers also said they were relieved coalition talks which had all but brought parliament to a halt, were finally over.  \par \par \uc2 But they also said the market impact of Thursday's deal was limited as they wanted action rather than a cabinet line-up.  \par \par \uc2 Yulia Tymoshenko, fired by the president last September after eight turbulent months in the office, is set to return as Ukraine's prime minister.  \par \par \uc2 She promised a predictable economic policy, but also vowed to review a gas deal with Russia under which Ukraine now pays nearly twice what it did before the New Year.  \par \par \uc2 "People are already tired of listening to this. It is not personalities, but concrete decisions that will have a market impact. That will determine investment inflow," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060622e26m00132\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
