\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Ukraine's c.bank aims to buy $2.1 bln by year-end  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Natalya Zinets  \par \uc2 493 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juni 2006\par 15:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds more comment, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, June 15 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants to buy $2.1 billion on the interbank market by the end of the year and has no plans to change its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, Anatoly Shapovalov, first deputy chairman, said on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The bank keeps close watch on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently, both buying and selling hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  within a 5.00-5.06 per dollar band since August 2005.  \par \par \uc2 Shapovalov said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wanted to replenish its reserves which sunk due to repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it suffered from uncertainty linked to an election in March and talks, still incomplete, on forming a government coalition.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $2.1 billion on the interbank market from January to April but turned to dollar purchases in May.  \par \par \uc2 "A lot lies in the political sphere. If a parliamentary coalition is created in the coming days, I think there are all conditions for us to buy these funds from the market by the end of the year," Shapovalov told Reuters.  \par \par \uc2 Politicians have been trying to put together a new coalition government for more than two months, but talks are stalled, largely due to disagreements over senior jobs.  \par \par \uc2 Parliament, which was elected on March 26 and has since held only three brief sittings, announced a further recess until next Tuesday to allow more time for the negotiations.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $47 million in the first two weeks of June compared with $244 million in May.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  <UAH=> has strengthened since the start of the month and is hovering at about 5.00 to the dollar. But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had no plans to change the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate and would continue to buy dollars at the current level.  \par \par \uc2 "If we look at the structure of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , we think there is no reason (to change the rate). Now the rate is balanced ... We do not plan to change the rate," he said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market again on Thursday, buying dollars at 5.00 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the fifth consecutive trading day, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Dollar inflows into Ukraine have increased due to active foreign borrowings by Ukrainian companies, rising hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  revenues by exporters and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  steps to reduce obligatory reserves for commercial banks, Shapovalov said.  \par \par \uc2 "The reason for the appreciation pressure of the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar comes from the sharp depreciation of the dollar against the euro," Raiffeisen Group said in a note.  \par \par \uc2 "Inflation also surprised to the downside, which means that the competitive position of Ukraine was developing much better than we had expected. We have changed our 3-month forecast for dollar/\b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 5.05."  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-UKRAINE-BANK (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|BNX|RNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060615e26f0014f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
