\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine's c. bank buys dollars for 2nd day  \b0\par\par\uc2 254 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juni 2006\par 16:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds comment)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, June 9 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday, buying dollars at 5.0 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the second day running, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which sold dollars through the first four months of the year, switched to purchases in May as political tensions dropped after a parliamentary election.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to step into the market on Thursday and Friday as demand for dollars was lower than usual on weaker business activity ahead of a long weekend in Ukraine. The country celebrates Trinity Day on Sunday and Monday.  \par \par \uc2 "Exporters might be selling dollars a bit more actively ahead of the long weekend. Also business is traditionally slower in the summer months," one dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 Exporters, a key source of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  revenue, also saw a revival last month, officials said.  \par \par \uc2 Prime Minister Yuri Yekhanurov has said growth in industrial production quickened to 10 percent in May compared with a 4.3 percent rise in the same month of 2005 due to expansion in the steel sector.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $244.1 million on the interbank market in May compared with sales of $232.8 million in April. It sold a total of $2.1 billion in January to April.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said most deals were struck between 5.005-5.010 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the dollar on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060609e2690018u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
