\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Ukraine c.bank says 5.05/$  \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia \highlight\uc2  rate "optimal"  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Natalya Zinets  \par \uc2 485 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Mai 2006\par 10:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds c. bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, May 31 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has no plans to change its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band and sees the current official \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate of 5.05 to the dollar as "optimal", a top bank official said on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 First deputy chairman Anatoly Shapovalov said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased $240 million on the interbank market in May, and forecast that dollar supply would exceed demand in the summer months.  \par \par \uc2 "We think that the rate 5.05 corresponds to the market situation in the best way today and that's why there is no volatility -- no devaluation or revaluation," Shapovalov told Reuters on the sidelines of a cabinet meeting.  \par \par \uc2 "The rates at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market, 5.0 and 5.06, also remain approved. Everything will remain within those limits which were approved."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently, both buying and selling dollars, to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  within 5.00-5.06 per dollar. It has defended the corridor since August 2005.  \par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars at 5.0 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the seventh time this month, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 "Dollar supply was obviously higher. The bulk of interbank deals were done at about 5.01," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had sold dollars earlier this year to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  against instability linked to a parliamentary election in March and subsequent talks on a government coalition.  \par \par \uc2 It sold $2.1 billion on the interbank market in January to April. In 2005, it bought $10.4 on the interbank market.  \par \par \uc2 DEBATE ON POLICY  \par \par \uc2 A fresh debate on policy opened this month after one of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's deputy chairmen told bankers in London that the bank intended to allow a more flexible exchange rate.  \par \par \uc2 The International Monetary Fund, private economists and even some government officials have repeatedly called on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to allow greater exchange rate flexibility.  \par \par \uc2 But \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chairman Volodymyr Stelmakh said this month that the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be kept stable.  \par \par \uc2 Any volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a very sensitive issue for the ex-Soviet state, where millions lost their life savings in failed monetary reforms in the early 1990s.  \par \par \uc2 Shapovalov reiterated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stand on the need for stability. He also said officials expected dollar supply to exceed demand in the summer months due to an inflow of funds from planned foreign borrowings.  \par \par \uc2 "On the whole, we think the country's payment balance will be positive (in 2006)," he said.  \par \par \uc2 "We have made an inquiry about planned borrowings -- $3.3 billion -- these are signed agreements. It will come in the second half of the year. Besides, there are protocols of intention for $2.9-3.2 billion," he said.  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-UKRAINE-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|BNX|RNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060531e25v000gs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
