\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine's c.bank buys dollars for 2nd time in week  \b0\par\par\uc2 290 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Mai 2006\par 13:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds details)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, May 25 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Thursday, buying dollars at 5.00 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the second time this week, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 "The inflow of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is here. Banks are attracting hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to issue loans to clients," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 "As there are rumours that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants to limit hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  credits, people may be more active now."  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials have previously said they were concerned over rapid growth in banking credits denominated in hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and were considering measures to limit it. But no concrete measures have been announced.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps close watch over the interbank market and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly, both buying and selling dollars, to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  within a corridor of 5.00-5.06 to the dollars.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's official rate, fixed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 5.05 to the dollar, has been unchanged for more than a year.  \par \par \uc2 "The market volumes are still not that big. There are no speculators who can support the market. That is why only the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can regulate even the smallest fluctuations in demand and supply," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars heavily in the first four months of 2006 to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  from political instability linked to a March parliamentary election and talks still proceeding over a coalition government.  \par \par \uc2 It sold $2.1 billion from January to April.  \par \par \uc2 Throughout 2005, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $10.4 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  six times to buy dollars so far in May.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060525e25p0010m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
