\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine c.bank head and deputy disagree on  \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 587 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Mai 2006\par 13:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds new \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, May 22 (Reuters) - The head of \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has put himself at variance with one of his deputies by saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be kept stable to guard against any sharp move on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market prompting a rise in inflation.  \par \par \uc2 Volodymyr Stelmakh's comments, published in the weekly Zerkalo Nedeli, opened fresh debate on the policy to be applied in overseeing the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Ukraine's markets.  \par \par \uc2 One of his deputies told the EBRD weekend meeting in London that Ukraine intended to allow more exchange rate flexibility.  \par \par \uc2 But the bank's policy of keeping the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within strict limits was confirmed again on Monday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , buying dollars at 5.0 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "I believe that our \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  must be stable," the weekly quoted Stelmakh as saying at a round table discussion.  \par \par \uc2 "And a rate that remains stable, such as exists now ... is a normal, objective thing."  \par \par \uc2 The hyrvnia has remained at a level of 5.05 to the dollar for the past year, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  routinely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since last August -- buying excess dollar supply at 5.0 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  and selling when required at 5.06.  \par \par \uc2 On Monday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars as per its normal practice at 5.0. Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the first since last Wednesday, did not reflect a marked new trend on the market and was aimed at adhering to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies.  \par \par \uc2 "Today was an ordinary trading day. There simply were greater volumes of dollars than there were buyers and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  took action by buying," said one dealer.  \par \par \uc2 Throughout 2005 the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $10.4 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 But it sold $2.1 billion in the first four months of 2006 to offset political instability triggered by a March parliamentary election and talks still to be concluded on forming a stable coalition government.  \par \par \uc2 EXPORT MARKETS, GAS PRICES  \par \par \uc2 Worsening export markets and a sharp increase in the price of Russian gas also contributed to higher demand for dollars.  \par \par \uc2 Stelmakh told the gathering that a \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation could trigger higher inflation.  \par \par \uc2 "Given the external challenges -- headed by energy prices, particularly gas -- our actions must be such not only to control inflation but to restrain it," he was quoted as saying.  \par \par \uc2 In London, bank deputy governor Oleksander Savchenko said once a coalition government was formed the bank would gradually move towards targeting inflation.  \par \par \uc2 "We treat the exchange rate as a managed float, but we'll do considerable exchange rate flexibility after the formation of the new government," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Savchenko has previously suggested the bank would gradually widen to between 4.98 and 5.1 to the dollar the boundaries within which it allows the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to move on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. The band is currently set at 5.0 to 5.06.  \par \par \uc2 Zerkalo Nedeli quoted Valery Geyets, head of the bank's council as saying Stelmakh's position enjoyed general support.  \par \par \uc2 "If we start adding instability on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to all our current difficulties, we will end up with inflation," he told the discussion.  \par \par \uc2 The outgoing government initially said it would contain inflation within 10 percent for 2006, but has revised the figure upward to 11.4 percent to take account of the nearly twofold increase in gas prices agreed with Russia in the New Year.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-UKRAINE-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060522e25m0012d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
