\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine c.bank buys dollars at 5.0  \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 361 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Mai 2006\par 15:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds quotes, details)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, May 17 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the foreign exchanges on Wednesday for the first time in a week, buying dollars at 5.0 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  in what traders said was a move to meet one-off factors not stabilise the market.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers expressed some surprise at the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and said it did not reflect any clear trend as most trades were conducted at about 5.0275/5.032. The bank, they said, had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to provide for a large operator unable to find buyers.  \par \par \uc2 "This was a surprise for us," said one dealer. "A big operator came onto the market late in the day and found no active buyers. There was no one, apart from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was engaged in nearly daily sales of dollars through the first four months of the year amid uncertainty over a March parliamentary election and difficult talks on forming a coalition government.  \par \par \uc2 Sales totalled $2.1 billion.  \par \par \uc2 But the market has since stabilised and this month the bank has even bought dollars on four occasions.  \par \par \uc2 The State Statistics Committee said on Tuesday Ukraine's total trade deficit, including goods and services, reached $769.1 million in the first quarter compared with a $1.6 billion surplus in the same period of 2005.  \par \par \uc2 Prime Minister Yuri Yekhanurov told a cabinet meeting on Wednesday he had asked the economy minister to prepare a report on the state of Ukraine's exports.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts have had some difficulty explaining the influx of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and have suggested it might amount to a correction after the election. Talks on forming a coalition of liberal forces that backed the 2004 "Orange Revolution" have hit a snag ahead of the new parliament's first sitting on May 25.  \par \par \uc2 "It is difficult to say what lies behind the inflow," said one dealer. "Clearly it is linked to investment of some sort. What happens now depends on moves to be made by the new parliament and government."  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060517e25h001b6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
