\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2  c. bank may widen  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\uc2  band-paper  \b0\par\par\uc2 377 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 2006\par 12:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, May 15 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may widen its \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  corridor to 4.98-5.1 per dollar for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Oleksander Savchenko, deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor, was quoted as saying.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently, both buying and selling dollars, to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  within 5.00-5.06 per dollar. It has defended the corridor since August, 2005.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has started to buy the hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  but it does not mean we can relax," Savchenko was quoted as saying in an interview published on Monday by business weekly Business.  \par \par \uc2 "Everything can change and we should be ready to broaden the corridor from 5-5.06 per dollar, maybe, to 4.98-5.1 per dollar."  \par \par \uc2 He provided no other details. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials were not immediately available for comment.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  nearly daily in the first four months of the year to sell dollars and defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  from political uncertainty linked to a parliamentary election in March. The bank sold $2.1 billion in January to April.  \par \par \uc2 The trend changed in May and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has started to buy dollars as exporters sold more U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to meet forthcoming tax payments. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  three times so far in May to sell dollars at 5.00 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Savchenko said the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to remain stable in the next two months but in future it could weaken due to higher gas prices or strengthen in the case of more favourable conditions for Ukraine's export-led economy.  \par \par \uc2 He did not elaborater.  \par \par \uc2 Ukraine's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  targets an average \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate of 5.00-5.20 per dollar this year but it wants to broaden the corridor to 4.95-5.25 per dollar from 2007.  \par \par \uc2 Savchenko also said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was concerned about the high growth of loans denominated in hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and issued by Ukrainian commercial banks.  \par \par \uc2 "Commercial banks issue credits in hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  more actively. They transfer their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risks to households ... If there is considerable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility, many families cannot afford to pay their hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans," he said.  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-UKRAINE-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060515e25f0015h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
