\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine's c. bank sells dollars for 3rd day  \b0\par\par\uc2 256 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 April 2006\par 14:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds quote, details)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, April 19 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Wednesday for a third trading day in a row, selling dollars at 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The bank keeps tight control over the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 It has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  nearly daily this year, save for a brief period in April, to defend it against instability linked to last month's parliamentary election and the stalled talks on forming a coalition government.  \par \par \uc2 "At the opening, the dollar was a bit expensive. Probably not only dealers but also some clients are a bit concerned, but there were rather a lot of sellers later in the day," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 "The gap was not very big, about $10-20 million."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is under pressure due to deadlock in talks over forming a new coalition government, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Politicians are trying to restore a liberal coalition that led Ukraine's "Orange Revolution" in 2004 but no concrete results have been achieved.  \par \par \uc2 Two main participants -- allies of President Viktor Yushchenko and former Prime Minister Yulia Tymoshenko -- accuse each other of bringing the talks to a standstill through unreasonable demands.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts expect a government to be formed in July.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has repeatedly said it is ready to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stability this year. It has spent more than $1.8 billion since the start of the year on \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060419e24j000x5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
