\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine's c. bank sells dollars for 2nd day  \b0\par\par\uc2 377 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 April 2006\par 15:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds dealers' comment)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, April 18 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the second trading day in a row on Tuesday as political uncertainty over a new government pressured the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already spent over $1.8 billion from its reserves since the start of the year, trying to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  from political volatility linked to a March parliamentary election and talks on a new coalition government.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars on Tuesday at 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the level it has been defending since August 2005.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is selling dollars but they have set limits. Why have they set limits? Probably, they have their own helicopter view from above," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 "A fast drop in reserves might be a cause for concern. Besides, sources to replenish them are not clearly seen."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  <UAH=> slipped in early trade to 5.067-5.0685 to the dollar from 5.064-5.0655 to the dollar on Monday but it gained some ground, trading up at 5.0610-5.0625 per dollar before the close.  \par \par \uc2 But dealers said the market was pessimistic and the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  was under pressure as there was no clarity in talks over the country's new government.  \par \par \uc2 "Two or three more days of continued uncertainty and the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  would slip below 5.07 to the dollar. Nobody can see sources to change the situation. Everything depends on politics," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 "The budget contains plans for privatisation revenues. It means hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflow. But privatisation will have to wait for a new government."  \par \par \uc2 Ukrainian politicians have been locked in talks over the government coalition for more than three weeks already, but with little sign of progress. Parliament is expected to gather for its first session in May and has about 2 months to form a coalition and name the government.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has repeatedly said it was ready to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability this year. Its hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves slipped to $17.3 billion on April 1 from about $19.4 billion in January.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060418e24i0011i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
