\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2  C.Bank in new post-election  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 283 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 April 2006\par 15:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds details, quotes)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, April 6 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  staged fresh \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Thursday, selling dollars at 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  in continued efforts to steady the Ukrainian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after a parliamentary election.  \par \par \uc2 "There were more dollars today than yesterday, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  still had to sell as demand exceeded supply," said one dealer.  \par \par \uc2 Market participants said deals were being struck at 5.061/5.0625.  \par \par \uc2 "Last month, things were a lot more tense. In April, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is selling about $15-20 million per day," said another dealer.  \par \par \uc2 The bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  nearly every day in March to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  from uncertainty linked to a March 26 parliamentary election and has done so every day this week except Tuesday.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  figures showed overall dollar sales on the first working day of the month -- April 3 -- had declined to $125.7 million from $177 million at the end of March.  \par \par \uc2 A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  statement issued on Wednesday said it had spent $724.4 million on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in March compared with $179 million in February and $938.7 million in January.  \par \par \uc2 Not all dealers agreed with \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  predictions that demand for dollars will decline once political parties agree on a coalition government.  \par \par \uc2 "We will have to wait and see," said one dealer. "Perhaps the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  knows something we don't. But I would not say that anything has changed in recent days to the extent that \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales will no longer be necessary."  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060406e246001zn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
