\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Ukraine's c.bank resumes dollar sales  \b0\par\par\uc2 293 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 April 2006\par 14:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds data on reserves)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, April 5 (Reuters) - Ukraine's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent more than $700 million supporting the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against political uncertainty in March and resumed its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday after a day's pause.  \par \par \uc2 The bank stayed away from the market on Monday, but \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  nearly every day last month to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the run-up to a March 26 parliamentary election.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement it spent $724.4 million on market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in March compared with $179 million in February and $938.7 million in January.  \par \par \uc2 Its gross hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell to $17.3 billion on March 31 from $18.3 billion at the end of February.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has repeatedly said it expects demand for dollars to fall sharply once politicians clinch a deal on a new coalition government.  \par \par \uc2 Five political parties will be represented in parliament but none has won enough votes to govern alone and talks on a coalition are now under way amid considerable secrecy.  \par \par \uc2 A party backing President Viktor Yushchenko says it expects a deal to be completed in May. Others are pressing for a quicker agreement.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said looming tax payments for the first quarter will also help the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cut the frequency of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "Demand still outpaces supply and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has to sell," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 "I expect it will have to continue dollar sales this week, but then the situation is likely to stabilise. Exporters who delayed dollar sales will be forced to proceed as they will have to pay profit tax."  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060405e245000xm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
