\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine c. bank in new dollar sales  \b0\par\par\uc2 274 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 April 2006\par 15:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds more quotes, details)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, April 3 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  staged fresh \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday, selling dollars at 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 "We can still see a lower dollar supply on the market," a dealer said. "The trend is unlikely to change in the short-term. Except probably in the summer when gas consumption falls, dollar demand will then also slip."  \par \par \uc2 Ukraine imports up to 80 percent of its energy resources, mostly from Russia. Prices for Russian natural gas have nearly doubled so far this year.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers also said political instability following a March 26 parliamentary election was putting pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  nearly every day this month.  \par \par \uc2 It has spent more than $1.5 billion to back the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the start of the year.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials hope demand for dollars will fall once politicians agree on a new coalition government.  \par \par \uc2 President Viktor Yushchenko said last week he hoped the parties that led Ukraine's "Orange Revolution" in 2004 would clinch a deal on a workable coalition within days.  \par \par \uc2 But some small parties which failed to clear a 3 percent barrier to qualify for a seat in parliament are demanding that election officials recount the votes. The poll was declared free and fair by international observers.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the challenges to the election result could prolong political uncertainty further.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the deals were done at between 5.0605 and 5.0625 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the dollar on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060403e24300173\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
