\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Agreement on govt would help  \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia \highlight\uc2 - \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2  c.bank  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Olena Horodetska  \par \uc2 502 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2006\par 12:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds c.bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,trader comment)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, March 30 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday it expected demand for dollars to fall sharply and the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to steady once political parties agree on a new coalition government.  \par \par \uc2 It said more dollars were now flowing into the country, where the bank has sold the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  nearly every day this month to calm a market unsettled by political tensions linked to last Sunday's parliamentary election.  \par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to step in on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market again, selling dollars at 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the rate it has been defending since last August.  \par \par \uc2 But Oleksander Savchenko, deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chairman, said he expected \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  would no longer be needed in about two weeks' time as the market trend was changing.  \par \par \uc2 "We are waiting for the election process to be completed... We believe it will be over once a coalition agreement is signed. We hope demand for hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will fall sharply," he told reporters.  \par \par \uc2 "We expect that in a month the trend of dollar sales will be replaced by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar purchases."  \par \par \uc2 Five political parties will be represented in a parliament which will now have powers to name a prime minister and some ministers. But no party has won an outright majority to govern alone and coalition talks are under way.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts expect the talks to be long and difficult. Parliament has 30 days to form a coalition and a further 30 days to agree on the government.  \par \par \uc2 "The elections were very stable, with no extremes. Businessmen are waiting for a devaluation but I would like to say this will not happen," he said. "Hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflow is now higher than at the end of last year."  \par \par \uc2 However, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said they had no impression that dollar supply was increasing.  \par \par \uc2 "The situation is pretty similar to what we have had for most of the month," a dealer said. "We do not feel dollar supply is growing. We also do not feel there are the necessary conditions for this in the near future."  \par \par \uc2 Exporters, a major source of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  revenue for Ukraine, have suffered due to lower world prices for steel and chemicals -- their major products -- and a nearly two-fold increase in prices for Russian natural gas.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has so far this year spent more than $1.5 billion from its reserves to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Savchencko said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  saw a slight rise in reserves and maintained its forecast for the average \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate at between 5.00-5.20 to the dollar for 2006.  \par \par \uc2 "We plan a rise in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. It is not big but it will be higher than the last year. The rate will be within the corridor approved by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said.  \par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Natalya Zinets)  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-UKRAINE-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060330e23u000qf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
