\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine's c. bank in new post-election dollar sales  \b0\par\par\uc2 205 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2006\par 14:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds details)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, March 28 (Reuters) - Ukraine's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars on Tuesday in a fresh post-election \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The bank has consistently sold dollars at 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the rate it has defended since August 2005.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is selling because it has no other choice. Demand for hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is rather high," a dealer said. "If last year money was coming into Ukraine from exports and loans, this year the direction of funds movement has changed."  \par \par \uc2 Hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflow into Ukraine has decreased since the start of the year due to weaker exports. But demand for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been sparked by political uncertainty linked to last Sunday's parliamentary election.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said a slow vote count and a delay in talks on a coalition government had only added to uncertainty.  \par \par \uc2 Five political parties are likely to be represented in parliament, according to returns from about 80 percent of the vote. None has won enough votes to govern alone and difficult coalition talks have been launched.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060328e23s000v1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\pi