\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine sells dollars as poll results awaited  \b0\par\par\uc2 352 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2006\par 15:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, dealer comment)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, March 27 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  resumed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday as markets waited for results of a parliamentary election for signals on future economic policy, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The bank has been selling dollars almost every day this month as political uncertainty in the run-up to Sunday's parliamentary election pushed up demand for hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The bank has consistently sold dollars at 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the rate it has defended since August 2005.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is selling at its unchanged rate of 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The gap is not big," a dealer said. "Clients will calm down when the economy will start working in a normal fashion again."  \par \par \uc2 Exit polls and incomplete returns from Sunday's parliamentary election showed the Russia-backed Regions Party of Viktor Yanukovich was leading.  \par \par \uc2 But a bloc led by former Prime Minister Yulia Tymoshenko was performing strongly in second place, putting her in a strong position to lead a future government coalition. Our Ukraine, which backs President Viktor Yushchenko, lay third.  \par \par \uc2 Tymoshenko and Yushchenko prepared for coalition talks but analysts doubted any quick deal was possible.  \par \par \uc2 "Talks will be long. There are loads of options and nobody will be in a hurry," a foreign banker in Kiev said.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will sit and wait to see how the political situation will develop. They will maintain the rate and continue to sell dollars at their usual rate. The rate will remain stable, at least until mid-summer."  \par \par \uc2 Hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflow into Ukraine has decreased since the start of the year due to weaker exports. But demand is being driven by higher prices for Russian natural gas and a desire by some foreign investors to curb their exposure.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been committed to keeping the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  at around 5.06 to the dollar in the near term. It sold over $1.5 billion from its reserves since the start of the year.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060327e23r0011z\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (Ukraine near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority) and hryvnia*\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \tr